{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"n2_000001","metadata":{"id":"n2_000001"},"source":["# R2-N2 — Google Colab Verified LR Bundle & Lock Packaging Verification\n","\n","**Project:** EchoProof  \n","**Task:** R2-N2 — Verified LR Bundle and Lock Packaging  \n","**Milestone:** GR2  \n","**Owner:** Nouman  \n","**Reviewer:** Usman  \n","**Dependencies:** R2-M1 (selected LR-B model), R2-N1 (LR end-to-end integration)  \n","\n","---\n","\n","## Executive Summary & Verification Scope\n","\n","This Google Colab notebook provides an independent, reproducible verification of the completed **R2-N2 packaging implementation** in EchoProof. It independently verifies the packaged Protocol B Logistic Regression bundle (`bundles/protocol_B_lr`), its cryptographic manifest (`bundle.json`), the formal Protocol B lock record (`locks/B_lock.json`), and their provenance link back to the provisional R2-M1 model artifacts (`runs/r2/r2_m1_20261106T140611Z/`).\n","\n","### Verification Objectives\n","1. **Original Artifact Integrity (Stage B):** Verify the existence, cryptographic digests, and run identity of original R2-M1 training artifacts without modifying or regenerating them.\n","2. **Bundle Component Integrity (Stage C):** Independently audit each component in `bundles/protocol_B_lr`, comparing byte counts and SHA-256 digests against `bundle.json`.\n","3. **Bundle Metadata Validation (Stage D):** Validate specification schema, model version, preprocessing hash, and decision rule via production `load_bundle()`.\n","4. **Lock Record Consistency (Stage E):** Validate `locks/B_lock.json` against the bundle, verifying split hash, feature schema, hyperparameters, selection metrics, panel metrics, and non-deployment limitations.\n","5. **Evidence & Provenance Traceability (Stage F):** Validate SHA-256 digests of R2-M1 `evidence.json` and referenced source code files, documenting execution boundaries and disclaimers.\n","6. **Production Packaged Loading (Stage G):** Load the packaged bundle through `load_lr_bundle()`, verifying `is_mock=False` and production readiness.\n","7. **Legacy Compatibility & Scoring Parity (Stage H):** Compare inference scores between packaged and legacy loaders on deterministic multi-chunk audio at strict numerical tolerance ($|\\Delta| < 10^{-9}$).\n","8. **Threshold Behavior (Stage I):** Verify default stored threshold inheritance, explicit threshold overrides, and rejection of invalid threshold contracts.\n","9. **Negative Integrity Sandboxes (Stage J):** Execute failure tests in temporary isolated copies to verify robust detection of corrupted components, modified metadata, tampered locks, and altered evidence.\n","10. **Regression Test Suite (Stage K):** Execute the repository's test suites (`test_r2_bundle.py`, `test_r2_lock.py`, `test_r2_n1_integration.py`).\n","11. **Verification Report Export (Stage L):** Compile dynamic results into `reports/r2/r2_n2_colab_bundle_verification_report.json`.\n","\n","**Runtime Requirement:** Standard Google Colab CPU runtime (GPU optional, not required). Execute all cells sequentially from top to bottom."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"n2_000002","metadata":{"id":"n2_000002"},"source":["## Stage A — Environment Setup & Project Root Discovery\n","\n","This stage detects whether the notebook is executing in Google Colab or a local workstation, mounts Google Drive if needed, discovers the project root, configures Python search paths, and performs a dependency audit.\n","\n","### Discovery Principles\n","- An unset or empty `ECHOPROOF_ROOT` is **never** treated as a valid candidate.\n","- Checks candidate locations in order: explicit environment variable, Google Drive project folders, and local workspace directories.\n","- Strictly validates candidates by checking for `pyproject.toml`, `src/echoproof`, `bundles/protocol_B_lr`, `locks/`, and `tests/`.\n","- Safe discovery: Never extracts archives or silently modifies existing project files.\n","- Initializes `STAGE_RESULTS` to dynamically track verification status across all stages without hardcoded values."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":43,"id":"n2_000003","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"n2_000003","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794109401772,"user_tz":-300,"elapsed":32,"user":{"displayName":"MUHAMMADNOUMAN FAZIL","userId":"00466758265510267650"}},"outputId":"e3c37a59-a782-4db8-cf14-c38eba992e06"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["[Colab] Google Colab runtime detected.\n","[Colab] Google Drive is already mounted.\n","[Root Validated] EchoProof project root: /content/drive/.shortcut-targets-by-id/1icE6vOFhCIuhCe6gfhFE2JI2yGHGBbMR/PAI&AIES Project\n","\n","[Environment Audit]\n","  python      : 3.13.18\n","  platform    : Linux-6.6.159+-x86_64-with-glibc2.39\n","  numpy       : 2.4.6\n","  scipy       : 1.16.3\n","  sklearn     : 1.6.1\n","  soundfile   : 0.14.0\n","  pyarrow     : 23.0.1\n","  in_colab    : True\n","  root        : /content/drive/.shortcut-targets-by-id/1icE6vOFhCIuhCe6gfhFE2JI2yGHGBbMR/PAI&AIES Project\n"]}],"source":["import os\n","import sys\n","import json\n","import time\n","import math\n","import hashlib\n","import platform\n","import subprocess\n","import tempfile\n","import shutil\n","from pathlib import Path\n","\n","os.chdir(ROOT)\n","# Tracking dictionary for dynamic stage-by-stage verification results\n","STAGE_RESULTS = {}\n","\n","# 1. Colab Detection & Google Drive Mounting\n","IN_COLAB = \"google.colab\" in sys.modules\n","if not IN_COLAB:\n","    try:\n","        import google.colab\n","        IN_COLAB = True\n","    except ImportError:\n","        IN_COLAB = False\n","\n","if IN_COLAB:\n","    print(\"[Colab] Google Colab runtime detected.\")\n","    drive_mount_path = Path(\"/content/drive\")\n","    if not (drive_mount_path / \"MyDrive\").exists():\n","        print(\"[Colab] Mounting Google Drive to /content/drive...\")\n","        from google.colab import drive\n","        drive.mount(str(drive_mount_path))\n","    else:\n","        print(\"[Colab] Google Drive is already mounted.\")\n","else:\n","    print(\"[Local/Workstation] Running in local workstation environment.\")\n","\n","# 2. Strict Project-Root Discovery & Validation\n","def is_valid_echoproof_root(candidate: Path) -> bool:\n","    \"\"\"Verify that candidate path contains the essential EchoProof R2 directory structure.\"\"\"\n","    try:\n","        cand = candidate.resolve()\n","        return (\n","            cand.is_dir()\n","            and (cand / \"pyproject.toml\").is_file()\n","            and (cand / \"src\" / \"echoproof\").is_dir()\n","            and (cand / \"bundles\" / \"protocol_B_lr\").is_dir()\n","            and (cand / \"locks\").is_dir()\n","            and (cand / \"tests\").is_dir()\n","        )\n","    except Exception:\n","        return False\n","\n","# Assemble candidate root locations in strict priority order\n","CANDIDATE_ROOTS = []\n","\n","env_root = os.environ.get(\"ECHOPROOF_ROOT\", \"\").strip()\n","if env_root:\n","    CANDIDATE_ROOTS.append(Path(env_root))\n","\n","if IN_COLAB:\n","    CANDIDATE_ROOTS.extend([\n","        Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/PAI&AIES Project\"),\n","        Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/EchoProof\"),\n","        Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/EchoProof-main\"),\n","        Path(\"/content/drive/My Drive/PAI&AIES Project\"),\n","        Path(\"/content/drive/My Drive/EchoProof\"),\n","        Path(\"/content/EchoProof\"),\n","        Path(\"/content/echoproof\"),\n","    ])\n","\n","cwd = Path.cwd().resolve()\n","CANDIDATE_ROOTS.extend([\n","    cwd,\n","    cwd.parent,\n","    cwd.parent.parent,\n","])\n","\n","ROOT = None\n","for cand in CANDIDATE_ROOTS:\n","    if is_valid_echoproof_root(cand):\n","        ROOT = cand.resolve()\n","        break\n","\n","if ROOT is None:\n","    error_msg = (\n","        \"CRITICAL ERROR: EchoProof project root could not be located!\\n\\n\"\n","        \"How to resolve this in Google Colab:\\n\"\n","        \"1. Ensure your EchoProof repository is uploaded to Google Drive, for example at:\\n\"\n","        \"   /content/drive/MyDrive/PAI&AIES Project\\n\"\n","        \"   or\\n\"\n","        \"   /content/drive/MyDrive/EchoProof\\n\"\n","        \"2. Alternatively, set ECHOPROOF_ROOT in an earlier cell:\\n\"\n","        \"   import os\\n\"\n","        \"   os.environ['ECHOPROOF_ROOT'] = '/path/to/EchoProof'\\n\"\n","        \"3. Valid EchoProof root must contain pyproject.toml, src/echoproof, bundles/protocol_B_lr, locks, tests.\\n\"\n","        f\"Checked candidate locations:\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(f\"  - {str(p)}\" for p in CANDIDATE_ROOTS)\n","    )\n","    STAGE_RESULTS[\"Stage A (Root Discovery)\"] = {\n","        \"status\": \"FAIL\",\n","        \"details\": \"Root directory not found among candidates\"\n","    }\n","    raise RuntimeError(error_msg)\n","\n","print(f\"[Root Validated] EchoProof project root: {ROOT}\")\n","\n","# 3. Configure Python Search Paths\n","sys.dont_write_bytecode = True\n","os.environ[\"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE\"] = \"1\"\n","for sub in [\"src\", \"\"]:\n","    p = str((ROOT / sub).resolve()) if sub else str(ROOT.resolve())\n","    if p not in sys.path:\n","        sys.path.insert(0, p)\n","os.environ[\"PYTHONPATH\"] = f\"{ROOT / 'src'}{os.pathsep}{ROOT}\"\n","\n","# 4. Dependency Audit\n","import numpy as np\n","import scipy\n","import sklearn\n","import soundfile as sf\n","\n","try:\n","    import pyarrow as pa\n","    pyarrow_ver = pa.__version__\n","except ImportError:\n","    pyarrow_ver = \"not installed\"\n","\n","ENV_AUDIT = {\n","    \"python\": platform.python_version(),\n","    \"platform\": platform.platform(),\n","    \"numpy\": np.__version__,\n","    \"scipy\": scipy.__version__,\n","    \"sklearn\": sklearn.__version__,\n","    \"soundfile\": sf.__version__,\n","    \"pyarrow\": pyarrow_ver,\n","    \"in_colab\": IN_COLAB,\n","    \"root\": str(ROOT),\n","}\n","\n","print(\"\\n[Environment Audit]\")\n","for k, v in ENV_AUDIT.items():\n","    print(f\"  {k:<12}: {v}\")\n","\n","STAGE_RESULTS[\"Stage A (Root Discovery)\"] = {\n","    \"status\": \"PASS\",\n","    \"details\": f\"Project root validated at {ROOT}, Python {platform.python_version()}\"\n","}"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"n2_000004","metadata":{"id":"n2_000004"},"source":["## Stage B — Original Artifact Verification\n","\n","This stage verifies the presence, cryptographic hashes, and metadata of the original **R2-M1 Protocol B Logistic Regression** model artifacts and training evidence before evaluating the packaged bundle:\n","- Model directory: `runs/r2/r2_m1_20261106T140611Z/model/` (`weights.npz`, `lr_model.json`)\n","- Training evidence: `runs/r2/r2_m1_20261106T140611Z/evidence.json`\n","\n","### Verification Principles\n","- Calculate independent SHA-256 digests and file sizes for each artifact.\n","- Inspect `evidence.json` for task identity, protocol, hyperparameter configuration, and feature schema.\n","- **Strict boundary:** Source artifacts must **never** be regenerated or modified."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":44,"id":"n2_000005","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"n2_000005","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794109408006,"user_tz":-300,"elapsed":99,"user":{"displayName":"MUHAMMADNOUMAN FAZIL","userId":"00466758265510267650"}},"outputId":"f3b19f64-3e5b-4da4-a772-e29be3280396"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["[Original Artifact Audit]\n","  Model Directory    : runs/r2/r2_m1_20261106T140611Z/model\n","  Evidence File      : runs/r2/r2_m1_20261106T140611Z/evidence.json\n","  weights.npz SHA    : 5a8e97c7356825f3d29e317f80fc0d053b61c44461556100dab1844f859ac4d3 (3392 bytes)\n","  lr_model.json SHA  : 784157878efdd8b647f25bd8f0db243e407a04822a316980093beeecc9907016 (2140 bytes)\n","  evidence.json SHA  : 04151701703f65a1fce3cfb1f849bd0fd024dad5fb4dba6627e00259368561ae (13656 bytes)\n","  Source Task        : R2-M1\n","  Protocol           : B\n","  Selected Order     : Trial 0\n","  Split SHA-256      : 0854de6b00ae059a858d60f18f95df3f1501f579ea3e2fdefbd8de076e2034d7\n","  Feature Schema SHA : fce2751a069d5d9b972ab772b1a76adf1a86bc12b13a07502cca171c86d50649\n"]}],"source":["ORIG_MODEL_DIR = ROOT / \"runs/r2/r2_m1_20261106T140611Z/model\"\n","ORIG_EVIDENCE_PATH = ROOT / \"runs/r2/r2_m1_20261106T140611Z/evidence.json\"\n","\n","assert ORIG_MODEL_DIR.is_dir(), f\"Original model directory not found: {ORIG_MODEL_DIR}\"\n","assert ORIG_EVIDENCE_PATH.is_file(), f\"Original evidence file not found: {ORIG_EVIDENCE_PATH}\"\n","\n","def compute_digest(path: Path) -> tuple[str, int]:\n","    data = path.read_bytes()\n","    return hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest(), len(data)\n","\n","orig_weights_hash, orig_weights_bytes = compute_digest(ORIG_MODEL_DIR / \"weights.npz\")\n","orig_meta_hash, orig_meta_bytes = compute_digest(ORIG_MODEL_DIR / \"lr_model.json\")\n","orig_evidence_hash, orig_evidence_bytes = compute_digest(ORIG_EVIDENCE_PATH)\n","\n","evidence_raw = json.loads(ORIG_EVIDENCE_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n","orig_task = evidence_raw.get(\"task\", \"unknown\")\n","orig_protocol = evidence_raw.get(\"protocol\", \"unknown\")\n","orig_selected_order = evidence_raw.get(\"selected_order\", -1)\n","orig_seed = evidence_raw.get(\"seed\", None)\n","orig_split_sha256 = evidence_raw.get(\"split_sha256\", \"\")\n","orig_feature_schema_hash = evidence_raw.get(\"feature_schema_hash\", \"\")\n","\n","print(\"[Original Artifact Audit]\")\n","print(f\"  Model Directory    : {ORIG_MODEL_DIR.relative_to(ROOT)}\")\n","print(f\"  Evidence File      : {ORIG_EVIDENCE_PATH.relative_to(ROOT)}\")\n","print(f\"  weights.npz SHA    : {orig_weights_hash} ({orig_weights_bytes} bytes)\")\n","print(f\"  lr_model.json SHA  : {orig_meta_hash} ({orig_meta_bytes} bytes)\")\n","print(f\"  evidence.json SHA  : {orig_evidence_hash} ({orig_evidence_bytes} bytes)\")\n","print(f\"  Source Task        : {orig_task}\")\n","print(f\"  Protocol           : {orig_protocol}\")\n","print(f\"  Selected Order     : Trial {orig_selected_order}\")\n","print(f\"  Split SHA-256      : {orig_split_sha256}\")\n","print(f\"  Feature Schema SHA : {orig_feature_schema_hash}\")\n","\n","assert orig_protocol == \"B\", f\"Expected Protocol B, got: {orig_protocol}\"\n","assert orig_selected_order == 0, f\"Expected selected Trial 0, got: {orig_selected_order}\"\n","assert orig_weights_bytes > 0, \"weights.npz is empty\"\n","assert orig_meta_bytes > 0, \"lr_model.json is empty\"\n","assert orig_evidence_bytes > 0, \"evidence.json is empty\"\n","\n","STAGE_RESULTS[\"Stage B (Original Artifacts)\"] = {\n","    \"status\": \"PASS\",\n","    \"details\": f\"Original R2-M1 artifacts intact (weights: {orig_weights_bytes}B, evidence: {orig_evidence_bytes}B, Protocol B)\"\n","}"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"n2_000006","metadata":{"id":"n2_000006"},"source":["## Stage C — Bundle Component Integrity & Original Artifact Comparison\n","\n","This stage verifies the packaged bundle structure at `bundles/protocol_B_lr/`.\n","It audits `bundle.json`, validates that each declared component exists on disk, computes independent byte counts and SHA-256 digests, compares them against the manifest, validates component paths against directory traversal / absolute paths, and directly compares original R2-M1 artifacts against their packaged counterparts.\n","\n","### Inspection & Comparison Criteria\n","- `bundle.json` exists and parses cleanly.\n","- Every component path is validated against traversal (`..`, `.`), backslashes (`\\`), absolute paths, and paths resolving outside the bundle directory.\n","- Every component declared in `components` exists on disk.\n","- Each component's byte count matches the recorded size.\n","- Each component's SHA-256 digest matches the recorded hash.\n","- Direct original-to-packaged comparison: Original R2-M1 `lr_model.json` and `weights.npz` must match their packaged counterparts in both SHA-256 hash AND byte count. Any mismatch must fail verification.\n","- No undeclared files exist in `model/` or the bundle directory."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":45,"id":"n2_000007","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"n2_000007","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794109411753,"user_tz":-300,"elapsed":47,"user":{"displayName":"MUHAMMADNOUMAN FAZIL","userId":"00466758265510267650"}},"outputId":"52bde98d-3d42-4eb1-e9af-c3d5bab5bb78"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["[Bundle Manifest Inspection: bundles/protocol_B_lr]\n","  bundle.json SHA-256 : 2c1faee6578d3a148292fbf71bb64419429a82f8dc2a0558b325d4a5393f6fae (689 bytes)\n","  Bundle ID           : bundle:r2-lr-protocol-b\n","  Model Version       : logistic_regression:B\n","  Declared Components : 2\n","  - Component: model/lr_model.json\n","      SHA-256 match : True (784157878efdd8b6...)\n","      Size match    : True (2140 bytes)\n","  - Component: model/weights.npz\n","      SHA-256 match : True (5a8e97c7356825f3...)\n","      Size match    : True (3392 bytes)\n","  Unexpected Files    : []\n","\n","[Direct Original-to-Packaged Artifact Comparison]\n","  - Comparing model/weights.npz:\n","      Original : SHA=5a8e97c7356825f3d29e317f80fc0d053b61c44461556100dab1844f859ac4d3 (3392 bytes)\n","      Packaged : SHA=5a8e97c7356825f3d29e317f80fc0d053b61c44461556100dab1844f859ac4d3 (3392 bytes)\n","      Match    : SHA=True, Size=True\n","  - Comparing model/lr_model.json:\n","      Original : SHA=784157878efdd8b647f25bd8f0db243e407a04822a316980093beeecc9907016 (2140 bytes)\n","      Packaged : SHA=784157878efdd8b647f25bd8f0db243e407a04822a316980093beeecc9907016 (2140 bytes)\n","      Match    : SHA=True, Size=True\n"]}],"source":["from pathlib import PurePosixPath\n","\n","BUNDLE_DIR = ROOT / \"bundles/protocol_B_lr\"\n","BUNDLE_JSON_PATH = BUNDLE_DIR / \"bundle.json\"\n","\n","assert BUNDLE_DIR.is_dir(), f\"Packaged bundle directory not found: {BUNDLE_DIR}\"\n","assert BUNDLE_JSON_PATH.is_file(), f\"bundle.json not found: {BUNDLE_JSON_PATH}\"\n","\n","bundle_json_bytes = BUNDLE_JSON_PATH.read_bytes()\n","bundle_metadata_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(bundle_json_bytes).hexdigest()\n","bundle_manifest = json.loads(bundle_json_bytes.decode(\"utf-8\"))\n","\n","declared_components = bundle_manifest.get(\"components\", {})\n","assert len(declared_components) > 0, \"No components declared in bundle.json\"\n","\n","print(f\"[Bundle Manifest Inspection: {BUNDLE_DIR.relative_to(ROOT)}]\")\n","print(f\"  bundle.json SHA-256 : {bundle_metadata_sha256} ({len(bundle_json_bytes)} bytes)\")\n","print(f\"  Bundle ID           : {bundle_manifest.get('bundle_id')}\")\n","print(f\"  Model Version       : {bundle_manifest.get('model_version')}\")\n","print(f\"  Declared Components : {len(declared_components)}\")\n","\n","# 1. Path Safety & Component Manifest Verification\n","component_audit = []\n","for rel_path, comp_info in sorted(declared_components.items()):\n","    # Path safety validation: no backslashes, not absolute, no traversal parts\n","    assert \"\\\\\" not in rel_path, f\"Component path contains invalid backslash: {rel_path}\"\n","    pure_p = PurePosixPath(rel_path)\n","    assert not pure_p.is_absolute(), f\"Component path cannot be absolute: {rel_path}\"\n","    assert not any(part in (\"..\", \".\", \"\") for part in pure_p.parts), f\"Component path contains invalid traversal: {rel_path}\"\n","\n","    file_path = BUNDLE_DIR / rel_path\n","    resolved_file = file_path.resolve()\n","    resolved_bundle = BUNDLE_DIR.resolve()\n","    assert resolved_file.is_relative_to(resolved_bundle), f\"Component resolves outside bundle directory: {rel_path}\"\n","    assert file_path.is_file(), f\"Declared component missing on disk: {file_path}\"\n","\n","    file_bytes = file_path.read_bytes()\n","    calc_sha = hashlib.sha256(file_bytes).hexdigest()\n","    calc_len = len(file_bytes)\n","\n","    decl_sha = comp_info.get(\"sha256\")\n","    decl_len = comp_info.get(\"bytes\")\n","\n","    sha_match = (calc_sha == decl_sha)\n","    len_match = (calc_len == decl_len)\n","\n","    component_audit.append({\n","        \"component\": rel_path,\n","        \"declared_sha256\": decl_sha,\n","        \"actual_sha256\": calc_sha,\n","        \"sha_match\": sha_match,\n","        \"declared_bytes\": decl_len,\n","        \"actual_bytes\": calc_len,\n","        \"len_match\": len_match,\n","    })\n","\n","    print(f\"  - Component: {rel_path}\")\n","    print(f\"      SHA-256 match : {sha_match} ({calc_sha[:16]}...)\")\n","    print(f\"      Size match    : {len_match} ({calc_len} bytes)\")\n","\n","    assert sha_match, f\"SHA-256 mismatch for component {rel_path}\"\n","    assert len_match, f\"Byte size mismatch for component {rel_path}\"\n","\n","# 2. Check for unexpected files in bundle directory\n","bundle_files = [p.relative_to(BUNDLE_DIR).as_posix() for p in BUNDLE_DIR.rglob(\"*\") if p.is_file()]\n","unexpected_files = [f for f in bundle_files if f != \"bundle.json\" and f not in declared_components]\n","print(f\"  Unexpected Files    : {unexpected_files}\")\n","assert len(unexpected_files) == 0, f\"Found undeclared files in bundle: {unexpected_files}\"\n","\n","# 3. Direct Original-to-Packaged Artifact Comparison\n","print(\"\\n[Direct Original-to-Packaged Artifact Comparison]\")\n","ORIG_TO_PKG_MAPPING = [\n","    (\"model/weights.npz\", ORIG_MODEL_DIR / \"weights.npz\", orig_weights_hash, orig_weights_bytes),\n","    (\"model/lr_model.json\", ORIG_MODEL_DIR / \"lr_model.json\", orig_meta_hash, orig_meta_bytes),\n","]\n","\n","orig_pkg_matches = []\n","for rel_path, orig_path, expected_hash, expected_bytes in ORIG_TO_PKG_MAPPING:\n","    pkg_file = BUNDLE_DIR / rel_path\n","    assert pkg_file.is_file(), f\"Packaged file missing for direct comparison: {pkg_file}\"\n","\n","    pkg_data = pkg_file.read_bytes()\n","    pkg_hash = hashlib.sha256(pkg_data).hexdigest()\n","    pkg_bytes = len(pkg_data)\n","\n","    hash_match = (pkg_hash == expected_hash)\n","    bytes_match = (pkg_bytes == expected_bytes)\n","\n","    print(f\"  - Comparing {rel_path}:\")\n","    print(f\"      Original : SHA={expected_hash} ({expected_bytes} bytes)\")\n","    print(f\"      Packaged : SHA={pkg_hash} ({pkg_bytes} bytes)\")\n","    print(f\"      Match    : SHA={hash_match}, Size={bytes_match}\")\n","\n","    assert hash_match, f\"Original-to-packaged SHA-256 mismatch for {rel_path}!\"\n","    assert bytes_match, f\"Original-to-packaged byte count mismatch for {rel_path}!\"\n","    orig_pkg_matches.append((rel_path, hash_match, bytes_match))\n","\n","STAGE_RESULTS[\"Stage C (Bundle Integrity)\"] = {\n","    \"status\": \"PASS\",\n","    \"details\": f\"All {len(declared_components)} components verified; path safety verified; direct original-to-packaged match confirmed (SHA & bytes)\"\n","}"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"n2_000008","metadata":{"id":"n2_000008"},"source":["## Stage D — Bundle Metadata Validation\n","\n","This stage uses EchoProof's production `load_bundle()` function from `echoproof.bundle` to load and validate the packaged bundle.\n","\n","### Validation Criteria\n","- Schema version: `1`\n","- Bundle ID: `bundle:r2-lr-protocol-b`\n","- Model version: `logistic_regression:B`\n","- Preprocessing hash: matches canonical `PREPROCESSING_HASH` (`879a76dabd6e486460c0d9bf40fe6cace934f993a5c0e6e09628a2640c1fa17a`)\n","- Decision rule: kind `threshold`, schema version `1`, default stored threshold `0.5`\n","- Classes: `genuine` (class 0) and `tts` (class 1)\n","- Resolved components: maps normalized paths to readable `Path` objects on disk"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":46,"id":"n2_000009","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"n2_000009","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794109416787,"user_tz":-300,"elapsed":33,"user":{"displayName":"MUHAMMADNOUMAN FAZIL","userId":"00466758265510267650"}},"outputId":"c9358032-a348-41d4-d78d-6de007d8ee07"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["[Production Bundle Loader Validation]\n","  Schema Version     : 1 (expected: 1)\n","  Bundle ID          : bundle:r2-lr-protocol-b\n","  Model Version      : logistic_regression:B\n","  Preprocessing Hash : 879a76dabd6e486460c0d9bf40fe6cace934f993a5c0e6e09628a2640c1fa17a\n","  Canonical Hash     : 879a76dabd6e486460c0d9bf40fe6cace934f993a5c0e6e09628a2640c1fa17a\n","  Decision Rule Kind : threshold\n","  Decision Threshold : 0.5\n","  Class 0 / Class 1  : genuine / tts\n","  Resolved Files     : ['model/lr_model.json', 'model/weights.npz']\n"]}],"source":["from echoproof.bundle import load_bundle, BUNDLE_SCHEMA_VERSION, ValidatedBundle\n","from echoproof.data.chunks import PREPROCESSING_HASH\n","\n","validated_bundle = load_bundle(BUNDLE_DIR)\n","assert isinstance(validated_bundle, ValidatedBundle), \"load_bundle did not return a ValidatedBundle instance\"\n","\n","spec = validated_bundle.spec\n","print(\"[Production Bundle Loader Validation]\")\n","print(f\"  Schema Version     : {spec.schema_version} (expected: {BUNDLE_SCHEMA_VERSION})\")\n","print(f\"  Bundle ID          : {spec.bundle_id}\")\n","print(f\"  Model Version      : {spec.model_version}\")\n","print(f\"  Preprocessing Hash : {spec.preprocessing_hash}\")\n","print(f\"  Canonical Hash     : {PREPROCESSING_HASH}\")\n","print(f\"  Decision Rule Kind : {spec.decision_rule.kind}\")\n","print(f\"  Decision Threshold : {spec.decision_rule.threshold}\")\n","print(f\"  Class 0 / Class 1  : {spec.class_0} / {spec.class_1}\")\n","print(f\"  Resolved Files     : {list(validated_bundle.components.keys())}\")\n","\n","assert spec.schema_version == BUNDLE_SCHEMA_VERSION, f\"Schema mismatch: {spec.schema_version}\"\n","assert spec.bundle_id == \"bundle:r2-lr-protocol-b\", f\"Bundle ID mismatch: {spec.bundle_id}\"\n","assert spec.model_version == \"logistic_regression:B\", f\"Model version mismatch: {spec.model_version}\"\n","assert spec.preprocessing_hash == PREPROCESSING_HASH, f\"Preprocessing hash mismatch: {spec.preprocessing_hash}\"\n","assert spec.decision_rule.kind == \"threshold\", f\"Rule kind mismatch: {spec.decision_rule.kind}\"\n","assert spec.decision_rule.threshold == 0.5, f\"Stored threshold mismatch: {spec.decision_rule.threshold}\"\n","assert spec.class_0 == \"genuine\" and spec.class_1 == \"tts\", \"Class mapping mismatch\"\n","\n","# Check component hashes stored in ValidatedBundle\n","for comp_path, comp_file in validated_bundle.components.items():\n","    assert comp_file.is_file(), f\"Component file path unresolvable: {comp_file}\"\n","    comp_hash = validated_bundle.component_hashes[comp_path]\n","    actual_hash = hashlib.sha256(comp_file.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n","    assert comp_hash == actual_hash, f\"Hash mismatch in ValidatedBundle: {comp_path}\"\n","\n","STAGE_RESULTS[\"Stage D (Bundle Metadata)\"] = {\n","    \"status\": \"PASS\",\n","    \"details\": f\"BundleSpecification validated (id={spec.bundle_id}, model={spec.model_version}, prep_hash matches)\"\n","}"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"n2_000010","metadata":{"id":"n2_000010"},"source":["## Stage E — Lock Record Validation\n","\n","This stage loads and validates `locks/B_lock.json` using the production validator `load_lock_record()` / `validate_lock_record()` from `echoproof.lock`.\n","\n","### Validation Scope\n","- Lock schema version: `1`, lock ID: `lock:protocol_b_lr_v1`, protocol: `B`.\n","- Cross-validation against the packaged bundle directory:\n","  - `bundle_metadata_hash` matches actual SHA-256 of `bundles/protocol_B_lr/bundle.json`.\n","  - Component manifest in the lock matches the bundle's components exactly (exact sets, byte sizes, and digests).\n","- Protocol B split hash: `0854de6b00ae059a858d60f18f95df3f1501f579ea3e2fdefbd8de076e2034d7`.\n","- Feature schema: 67 features, schema hash `fce2751a069d5d9b972ab772b1a76adf1a86bc12b13a07502cca171c86d50649`.\n","- Selected model: logistic regression, Trial 0, C=0.01, seed=42, class_weight='none', max_iter=2000.\n","- Selection metrics & evaluation panels: all rates and probabilities within $[0.0, 1.0]$.\n","- Limitations & test-access audit: explicit `NOT_DEPLOYMENT_APPROVED` warning, documented generalization degradation on unseen generator (XTTS), and `audit_status == \"partially_verified\"`."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":47,"id":"n2_000011","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"n2_000011","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794109420467,"user_tz":-300,"elapsed":50,"user":{"displayName":"MUHAMMADNOUMAN FAZIL","userId":"00466758265510267650"}},"outputId":"4cb1b46e-1823-4988-8778-77f3281921fd"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["[Production Lock Record Validation]\n","  Schema Version     : 1 (expected: 1)\n","  Lock ID            : lock:protocol_b_lr_v1\n","  Protocol           : B\n","  Bundle ID          : bundle:r2-lr-protocol-b\n","  Bundle Meta SHA    : 2c1faee6578d3a148292fbf71bb64419429a82f8dc2a0558b325d4a5393f6fae\n","  Split SHA-256      : 0854de6b00ae059a858d60f18f95df3f1501f579ea3e2fdefbd8de076e2034d7\n","  Feature Count      : 67\n","  Feature Schema SHA : fce2751a069d5d9b972ab772b1a76adf1a86bc12b13a07502cca171c86d50649\n","  Prep Hash          : 879a76dabd6e486460c0d9bf40fe6cace934f993a5c0e6e09628a2640c1fa17a\n","  Selected Model     : logistic_regression (logistic_regression:B)\n","  Hyperparameters    : {'C': 0.01, 'class_weight': 'none', 'max_iter': 2000, 'seed': 42}\n","  Selection Accuracy : 0.7205\n","  Selection Macro F1 : 0.6923479110340605\n","  Selection ROC-AUC  : 0.8202773333333333\n","  Selection EER      : 0.2533333333333333\n","  Known Generators   : ['melo', 'vits'] (ROC-AUC=0.9674, F1=0.9008)\n","  Unseen Generator   : ['xtts'] (ROC-AUC=0.5261, F1=0.4190)\n","  Audit Status       : partially_verified\n","  Test Accessed      : False\n"]}],"source":["from echoproof.lock import (\n","    LOCK_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n","    PROTOCOL_B_SPLIT_HASH,\n","    EXPECTED_FEATURE_SCHEMA_HASH,\n","    load_lock_record,\n","    validate_lock_record,\n","    LockError\n",")\n","\n","LOCK_PATH = ROOT / \"locks/B_lock.json\"\n","assert LOCK_PATH.is_file(), f\"Lock file not found: {LOCK_PATH}\"\n","\n","# Load and validate lock record cross-referenced with the packaged bundle\n","lock_record = load_lock_record(LOCK_PATH, bundle_dir=BUNDLE_DIR)\n","\n","print(\"[Production Lock Record Validation]\")\n","print(f\"  Schema Version     : {lock_record.get('schema_version')} (expected: {LOCK_SCHEMA_VERSION})\")\n","print(f\"  Lock ID            : {lock_record.get('lock_id')}\")\n","print(f\"  Protocol           : {lock_record.get('protocol')}\")\n","print(f\"  Bundle ID          : {lock_record.get('bundle', {}).get('bundle_id')}\")\n","print(f\"  Bundle Meta SHA    : {lock_record.get('bundle', {}).get('bundle_metadata_hash')}\")\n","print(f\"  Split SHA-256      : {lock_record.get('split', {}).get('split_hash')}\")\n","print(f\"  Feature Count      : {lock_record.get('feature_schema', {}).get('feature_count')}\")\n","print(f\"  Feature Schema SHA : {lock_record.get('feature_schema', {}).get('feature_schema_hash')}\")\n","print(f\"  Prep Hash          : {lock_record.get('feature_schema', {}).get('preprocessing_hash')}\")\n","\n","# Assert core identities\n","assert lock_record[\"schema_version\"] == LOCK_SCHEMA_VERSION\n","assert lock_record[\"protocol\"] == \"B\"\n","assert lock_record[\"bundle\"][\"bundle_id\"] == \"bundle:r2-lr-protocol-b\"\n","assert lock_record[\"bundle\"][\"bundle_metadata_hash\"] == bundle_metadata_sha256\n","assert lock_record[\"split\"][\"split_hash\"] == PROTOCOL_B_SPLIT_HASH\n","assert lock_record[\"feature_schema\"][\"feature_count\"] == 67\n","assert lock_record[\"feature_schema\"][\"feature_schema_hash\"] == EXPECTED_FEATURE_SCHEMA_HASH\n","assert lock_record[\"feature_schema\"][\"preprocessing_hash\"] == PREPROCESSING_HASH\n","\n","# Selected model & hyperparameters\n","sel_model = lock_record.get(\"selected_model\", {})\n","print(f\"  Selected Model     : {sel_model.get('architecture')} ({sel_model.get('model_version')})\")\n","print(f\"  Hyperparameters    : {sel_model.get('hyperparameters')}\")\n","assert sel_model.get(\"trial_order\") == 0\n","assert sel_model.get(\"hyperparameters\", {}).get(\"C\") == 0.01\n","assert sel_model.get(\"hyperparameters\", {}).get(\"seed\") == 42\n","assert sel_model.get(\"hyperparameters\", {}).get(\"class_weight\") == \"none\"\n","\n","# Selection metrics\n","sel_metrics = lock_record.get(\"selection_metrics\", {})\n","print(f\"  Selection Accuracy : {sel_metrics.get('accuracy')}\")\n","print(f\"  Selection Macro F1 : {sel_metrics.get('macro_f1')}\")\n","print(f\"  Selection ROC-AUC  : {sel_metrics.get('roc_auc')}\")\n","print(f\"  Selection EER      : {sel_metrics.get('eer')}\")\n","assert 0.0 <= sel_metrics.get(\"accuracy\", -1) <= 1.0\n","assert 0.0 <= sel_metrics.get(\"macro_f1\", -1) <= 1.0\n","assert 0.0 <= sel_metrics.get(\"roc_auc\", -1) <= 1.0\n","assert 0.0 <= sel_metrics.get(\"eer\", -1) <= 1.0\n","assert sel_metrics.get(\"recordings\") == 2000\n","\n","# Evaluation panels\n","panels = lock_record.get(\"evaluation_panels\", {})\n","known_panel = panels.get(\"known_generators\", {})\n","unseen_panel = panels.get(\"unseen_generators\", {})\n","print(f\"  Known Generators   : {known_panel.get('generators')} (ROC-AUC={known_panel.get('roc_auc'):.4f}, F1={known_panel.get('macro_f1'):.4f})\")\n","print(f\"  Unseen Generator   : {unseen_panel.get('generators')} (ROC-AUC={unseen_panel.get('roc_auc'):.4f}, F1={unseen_panel.get('macro_f1'):.4f})\")\n","assert known_panel.get(\"roc_auc\", 0) > 0.90\n","assert unseen_panel.get(\"roc_auc\", 0) < 0.60, \"Expected documented generalization drop on XTTS\"\n","\n","# Limitations and Test Access Audit\n","limitations = lock_record.get(\"limitations\", [])\n","assert any(\"NOT_DEPLOYMENT_APPROVED\" in l for l in limitations)\n","assert any(\"GENERALIZATION_FAILURE\" in l for l in limitations)\n","\n","audit = lock_record.get(\"test_access_audit\", {})\n","print(f\"  Audit Status       : {audit.get('audit_status')}\")\n","print(f\"  Test Accessed      : {audit.get('test_partition_accessed')}\")\n","assert audit.get(\"audit_status\") == \"partially_verified\"\n","assert audit.get(\"test_partition_accessed\") is False\n","assert len(audit.get(\"verified_history\", [])) >= 3\n","assert len(audit.get(\"unverified_history\", [])) >= 1\n","\n","STAGE_RESULTS[\"Stage E (Lock Record Validation)\"] = {\n","    \"status\": \"PASS\",\n","    \"details\": f\"B_lock.json validated against bundle (split_hash={PROTOCOL_B_SPLIT_HASH[:12]}..., audit_status=partially_verified)\"\n","}"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"n2_000012","metadata":{"id":"n2_000012"},"source":["## Stage F — Evidence and Provenance Traceability\n","\n","This stage verifies the cryptographic link between the original training evidence (`runs/r2/r2_m1_20261106T140611Z/evidence.json`) and the formal lock record (`locks/B_lock.json`).\n","\n","### Provenance Audit Scope\n","1. Compare the independent SHA-256 digest of `evidence.json` with `evidence_references.r2_m1_evidence_sha256` in the lock.\n","2. Cross-verify referenced source code digests (`lr_detector.py`, `metrics.py`, `r2_m1_lr.py`). Require all 3 source files to exist and their hashes to match either raw-byte or LF-normalized SHA-256. A missing file or hash mismatch will fail Stage F.\n","3. Verify run and task identity consistency:\n","   - Exact bundle source run ID: `r2_m1_20261106T140611Z` (exact timestamped training run artifact directory).\n","   - Exact lock and evidence task ID: `R2-M1` (milestone task identifier).\n","   - Document that these identify the same source task at complementary levels of granularity; do not require the strings to be identical.\n","4. The final provenance result strictly depends on all these checks passing.\n","5. Explicitly document limitations and audit boundaries."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":48,"id":"n2_000013","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"n2_000013","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794109425651,"user_tz":-300,"elapsed":34,"user":{"displayName":"MUHAMMADNOUMAN FAZIL","userId":"00466758265510267650"}},"outputId":"2ceab692-7bee-4069-9ac8-50457521469c"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["[Evidence & Provenance Audit]\n","  Evidence File Path : runs/r2/r2_m1_20261106T140611Z/evidence.json\n","  Recorded SHA-256   : 04151701703f65a1fce3cfb1f849bd0fd024dad5fb4dba6627e00259368561ae\n","  Actual SHA-256     : 04151701703f65a1fce3cfb1f849bd0fd024dad5fb4dba6627e00259368561ae\n","  Hash Match         : True\n","\n","[Referenced Source Code Integrity]\n","  - lr_detector.py  : match=True (exact raw match)\n","  - metrics.py      : match=True (exact raw match)\n","  - r2_m1_lr.py     : match=True (exact raw match)\n","\n","[Run Identity Verification]\n","  Bundle Source Run ID : r2_m1_20261106T140611Z\n","  Lock Source Run ID   : R2-M1\n","  Evidence Task ID     : R2-M1\n","  Identity Provenance  : Verified consistent.\n","  Note: 'R2-M1' identifies the milestone task level (in evidence.json and B_lock.json),\n","  while 'r2_m1_20261106T140611Z' identifies the exact timestamped training run artifact directory.\n","  Both refer to the same source experiment at complementary levels of granularity.\n","\n","[Provenance Boundaries & Methodological Disclaimers]\n","- Test partition exclusion during R2-M1 training was verified by codebase audit and evidence inspection.\n","- Independent proof that developer workstations or external processes never read test files cannot\n","  be cryptographically established post-hoc without tamper-proof hardware enclaves.\n","- Audit status remains 'partially_verified' in strict adherence to scientific integrity principles.\n"]}],"source":["evidence_refs = lock_record.get(\"evidence_references\", {})\n","lock_evidence_sha = evidence_refs.get(\"r2_m1_evidence_sha256\")\n","assert lock_evidence_sha == orig_evidence_hash, (\n","    f\"Evidence hash mismatch! Lock has {lock_evidence_sha}, actual file has {orig_evidence_hash}\"\n",")\n","\n","print(\"[Evidence & Provenance Audit]\")\n","print(f\"  Evidence File Path : {evidence_refs.get('r2_m1_evidence_path')}\")\n","print(f\"  Recorded SHA-256   : {lock_evidence_sha}\")\n","print(f\"  Actual SHA-256     : {orig_evidence_hash}\")\n","print(f\"  Hash Match         : {lock_evidence_sha == orig_evidence_hash}\")\n","\n","# 1. Audit Source Code SHA-256 References (All 3 required to exist and match)\n","src_refs = evidence_refs.get(\"source_code_sha256\", {})\n","source_audit = {}\n","\n","REQUIRED_SOURCE_FILES = [\"lr_detector.py\", \"metrics.py\", \"r2_m1_lr.py\"]\n","KNOWN_SOURCE_PATHS = {\n","    \"lr_detector.py\": ROOT / \"src/echoproof/models/lr_detector.py\",\n","    \"metrics.py\": ROOT / \"src/echoproof/evaluation/metrics.py\",\n","    \"r2_m1_lr.py\": ROOT / \"scripts/r2_m1_lr.py\",\n","}\n","\n","print(\"\\n[Referenced Source Code Integrity]\")\n","for name in REQUIRED_SOURCE_FILES:\n","    assert name in src_refs, f\"Evidence references missing expected source entry: {name}\"\n","    expected_hash = src_refs[name]\n","    path = KNOWN_SOURCE_PATHS.get(name)\n","\n","    # Require file to exist on disk\n","    assert path is not None and path.is_file(), f\"Required source file missing on disk: {name} (expected at {path})\"\n","\n","    raw_bytes = path.read_bytes()\n","    raw_hash = hashlib.sha256(raw_bytes).hexdigest()\n","    lf_hash = hashlib.sha256(raw_bytes.replace(b\"\\r\\n\", b\"\\n\")).hexdigest()\n","    matches_raw = (raw_hash == expected_hash)\n","    matches_lf = (lf_hash == expected_hash)\n","    hash_matched = (matches_raw or matches_lf)\n","\n","    note = \"exact raw match\" if matches_raw else (\"matches with LF newline normalization\" if matches_lf else \"mismatch\")\n","    source_audit[name] = {\n","        \"expected\": expected_hash,\n","        \"raw_hash\": raw_hash,\n","        \"lf_hash\": lf_hash,\n","        \"match\": hash_matched,\n","        \"note\": note,\n","    }\n","    print(f\"  - {name:<16}: match={hash_matched} ({note})\")\n","    assert hash_matched, f\"Source code hash mismatch for {name}: expected {expected_hash}, raw={raw_hash}, lf={lf_hash}\"\n","\n","assert len(source_audit) == 3, f\"Expected 3 audited source files, got {len(source_audit)}\"\n","assert all(v[\"match\"] for v in source_audit.values()), \"Not all referenced source files passed integrity checks!\"\n","\n","# 2. Check Run Identity & Task Identifier Consistency\n","lock_run_id = lock_record[\"selected_model\"][\"source_run_id\"]\n","bundle_run_id = bundle_manifest.get(\"extra\", {}).get(\"source_run_id\")\n","evidence_task = evidence_raw.get(\"task\")\n","\n","print(f\"\\n[Run Identity Verification]\")\n","print(f\"  Bundle Source Run ID : {bundle_run_id}\")\n","print(f\"  Lock Source Run ID   : {lock_run_id}\")\n","print(f\"  Evidence Task ID     : {evidence_task}\")\n","\n","# Exact bundle source run ID check\n","assert bundle_run_id == \"r2_m1_20261106T140611Z\", (\n","    f\"Bundle source run ID mismatch: expected 'r2_m1_20261106T140611Z', got {bundle_run_id!r}\"\n",")\n","\n","# Exact lock and evidence task ID checks\n","assert lock_run_id == \"R2-M1\", (\n","    f\"Lock source run ID mismatch: expected 'R2-M1', got {lock_run_id!r}\"\n",")\n","assert evidence_task == \"R2-M1\", (\n","    f\"Evidence task identifier mismatch: expected 'R2-M1', got {evidence_task!r}\"\n",")\n","\n","print(\"  Identity Provenance  : Verified consistent.\")\n","print(\"  Note: 'R2-M1' identifies the milestone task level (in evidence.json and B_lock.json),\")\n","print(\"  while 'r2_m1_20261106T140611Z' identifies the exact timestamped training run artifact directory.\")\n","print(\"  Both refer to the same source experiment at complementary levels of granularity.\")\n","\n","# Document Unverified Claims\n","print(\"\\n[Provenance Boundaries & Methodological Disclaimers]\")\n","print(\"- Test partition exclusion during R2-M1 training was verified by codebase audit and evidence inspection.\")\n","print(\"- Independent proof that developer workstations or external processes never read test files cannot\")\n","print(\"  be cryptographically established post-hoc without tamper-proof hardware enclaves.\")\n","print(\"- Audit status remains 'partially_verified' in strict adherence to scientific integrity principles.\")\n","\n","# Ensure final stage result depends strictly on all checks passing\n","all_provenance_passed = (\n","    (lock_evidence_sha == orig_evidence_hash)\n","    and (len(source_audit) == 3)\n","    and all(v[\"match\"] for v in source_audit.values())\n","    and (bundle_run_id == \"r2_m1_20261106T140611Z\")\n","    and (lock_run_id == \"R2-M1\")\n","    and (evidence_task == \"R2-M1\")\n",")\n","assert all_provenance_passed, \"Provenance verification failed\"\n","\n","STAGE_RESULTS[\"Stage F (Evidence Provenance)\"] = {\n","    \"status\": \"PASS\" if all_provenance_passed else \"FAIL\",\n","    \"details\": f\"Evidence SHA-256 verified ({orig_evidence_hash[:16]}...), 3/3 source files matched, run IDs verified ('R2-M1' / 'r2_m1_20261106T140611Z')\"\n","}"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"n2_000014","metadata":{"id":"n2_000014"},"source":["## Stage G — Production Packaged Loading via Shared Pipeline\n","\n","This stage tests loading the packaged bundle using the actual production entry point `load_lr_bundle(\"bundles/protocol_B_lr\")` from `echoproof.inference`.\n","\n","### Verification Criteria\n","- `LoadedBundle` returns `is_mock=False`.\n","- `score_type` is `\"model_score\"`.\n","- `spec.model_version` is `\"logistic_regression:B\"`.\n","- `spec.preprocessing_hash` matches canonical `PREPROCESSING_HASH`.\n","- Default stored threshold `0.5` is inherited when no explicit threshold override is supplied.\n","- Scorer callable (`scorer`) and aggregator callable (`aggregate`) are successfully loaded and ready for chunk processing."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":49,"id":"n2_000015","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"n2_000015","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794109430155,"user_tz":-300,"elapsed":33,"user":{"displayName":"MUHAMMADNOUMAN FAZIL","userId":"00466758265510267650"}},"outputId":"1badfa8e-ad2d-4889-af50-3732af438a37"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["[Production Packaged Bundle Loading Output]\n","  Bundle ID          : bundle:r2-lr-protocol-b\n","  Model Version      : logistic_regression:B\n","  Score Type         : model_score\n","  Is Mock            : False\n","  Preprocessing Hash : 879a76dabd6e486460c0d9bf40fe6cace934f993a5c0e6e09628a2640c1fa17a\n","  Decision Threshold : 0.5\n","  Scorer Callable    : True\n","  Aggregate Callable : True\n"]}],"source":["from echoproof.inference import load_lr_bundle, LoadedBundle\n","\n","loaded_pkg_bundle = load_lr_bundle(BUNDLE_DIR)\n","assert isinstance(loaded_pkg_bundle, LoadedBundle), \"load_lr_bundle did not return LoadedBundle\"\n","\n","print(\"[Production Packaged Bundle Loading Output]\")\n","print(f\"  Bundle ID          : {loaded_pkg_bundle.spec.bundle_id}\")\n","print(f\"  Model Version      : {loaded_pkg_bundle.spec.model_version}\")\n","print(f\"  Score Type         : {loaded_pkg_bundle.score_type}\")\n","print(f\"  Is Mock            : {loaded_pkg_bundle.is_mock}\")\n","print(f\"  Preprocessing Hash : {loaded_pkg_bundle.spec.preprocessing_hash}\")\n","print(f\"  Decision Threshold : {loaded_pkg_bundle.spec.decision_rule.threshold}\")\n","print(f\"  Scorer Callable    : {callable(loaded_pkg_bundle.scorer)}\")\n","print(f\"  Aggregate Callable : {callable(loaded_pkg_bundle.aggregate)}\")\n","\n","assert loaded_pkg_bundle.is_mock is False, \"Loaded bundle must not be mock\"\n","assert loaded_pkg_bundle.score_type == \"model_score\", f\"Unexpected score type: {loaded_pkg_bundle.score_type}\"\n","assert loaded_pkg_bundle.spec.model_version == \"logistic_regression:B\", f\"Unexpected model version: {loaded_pkg_bundle.spec.model_version}\"\n","assert loaded_pkg_bundle.spec.preprocessing_hash == PREPROCESSING_HASH, \"Preprocessing hash mismatch\"\n","assert loaded_pkg_bundle.spec.decision_rule.threshold == 0.5, f\"Stored threshold not inherited: {loaded_pkg_bundle.spec.decision_rule.threshold}\"\n","assert callable(loaded_pkg_bundle.scorer), \"Scorer must be callable\"\n","assert callable(loaded_pkg_bundle.aggregate), \"Aggregate must be callable\"\n","\n","STAGE_RESULTS[\"Stage G (Packaged Bundle Loading)\"] = {\n","    \"status\": \"PASS\",\n","    \"details\": f\"load_lr_bundle loaded successfully (is_mock=False, threshold=0.5, model={loaded_pkg_bundle.spec.model_version})\"\n","}"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"n2_000016","metadata":{"id":"n2_000016"},"source":["## Stage H — Legacy Compatibility and Scoring Parity\n","\n","This stage loads the provisional R2-M1 model through the legacy loader path (`load_lr_bundle(ORIG_MODEL_DIR)`) and compares its scoring output against the packaged bundle (`load_lr_bundle(BUNDLE_DIR)`).\n","\n","### Multi-Chunk Audio Preparation & Parity Principles\n","- Generates a deterministic 6.0-second synthetic audio recording at 16 kHz (96,000 samples).\n","- With canonical 4.0-second evaluation windows and a 2.0-second stride, this yields exactly **2 evaluation chunks**:\n","  - Window 0: $[0, 64000]$ (0.0 s to 4.0 s)\n","  - Window 1: $[32000, 96000]$ (2.0 s to 6.0 s)\n","- Feeds identical audio bytes through both inference pipelines (`analyze()`).\n","- Verifies bit-for-bit / high-precision floating-point score equality ($|\\Delta| \\le 10^{-9}$) across recording-level scores and individual chunk scores.\n","- **Methodological Boundary:** This deterministic synthetic audio is purpose-generated for pipeline and mathematical parity verification. It does not measure real-world deepfake detection accuracy or generalization on human speech."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":50,"id":"n2_000017","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"n2_000017","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794109434522,"user_tz":-300,"elapsed":222,"user":{"displayName":"MUHAMMADNOUMAN FAZIL","userId":"00466758265510267650"}},"outputId":"5193f33e-0468-4e59-d7ef-98fc928655cd"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["[Inference Parity: Packaged Bundle vs Legacy Model Directory]\n","  Duration           : 6.0 s (192044 bytes WAV)\n","  Canonical Chunks   : 2\n","  Packaged Score     : 0.999958552420 (assessment: 'synthetic')\n","  Legacy Score       : 0.999958552420 (assessment: 'synthetic')\n","  Absolute Delta     : 0.00e+00\n","  Exact Bitwise Equiv: True\n","  Max Chunk Delta    : 0.00e+00\n","  Chunk Scores (Pkg) : [0.99995941, 0.9999577]\n","  Chunk Scores (Leg) : [0.99995941, 0.9999577]\n"]}],"source":["import io\n","from echoproof.inference import analyze\n","from echoproof.data.chunks import eval_windows, SAMPLE_RATE, WINDOW_SECONDS, STRIDE_SECONDS\n","\n","# 1. Load legacy model directory\n","loaded_legacy_bundle = load_lr_bundle(ORIG_MODEL_DIR)\n","assert loaded_legacy_bundle.is_mock is False, \"Legacy bundle must not be mock\"\n","\n","# 2. Generate deterministic multi-chunk audio (6.0s duration = 2 canonical windows)\n","DURATION_SEC = 6.0\n","n_samples = int(round(DURATION_SEC * SAMPLE_RATE))\n","t = np.arange(n_samples) / SAMPLE_RATE\n","\n","rng = np.random.default_rng(42)\n","audio_waveform = (\n","    0.30 * np.sin(2 * np.pi * 220.0 * t) +\n","    0.15 * np.sin(2 * np.pi * 440.0 * t) +\n","    0.05 * np.sin(2 * np.pi * 880.0 * t) +\n","    0.01 * rng.standard_normal(len(t))\n",").astype(np.float32)\n","\n","audio_buffer = io.BytesIO()\n","sf.write(audio_buffer, audio_waveform, SAMPLE_RATE, format=\"WAV\", subtype=\"PCM_16\")\n","SYNTHETIC_AUDIO_BYTES = audio_buffer.getvalue()\n","\n","expected_windows = eval_windows(n_samples)\n","assert len(expected_windows) >= 2, f\"Expected >= 2 evaluation chunks, got {len(expected_windows)}\"\n","\n","# 3. Execute inference through both packaged and legacy loaders\n","res_pkg = analyze(SYNTHETIC_AUDIO_BYTES, loaded_pkg_bundle)\n","res_leg = analyze(SYNTHETIC_AUDIO_BYTES, loaded_legacy_bundle)\n","\n","s_pkg = res_pkg.result.score\n","s_leg = res_leg.result.score\n","score_diff = abs(s_pkg - s_leg)\n","exact_match = (s_pkg == s_leg)\n","\n","chunk_diffs = [abs(a - b) for a, b in zip(res_pkg.chunk_scores, res_leg.chunk_scores)]\n","max_chunk_diff = max(chunk_diffs) if chunk_diffs else 0.0\n","\n","print(\"[Inference Parity: Packaged Bundle vs Legacy Model Directory]\")\n","print(f\"  Duration           : {DURATION_SEC:.1f} s ({len(SYNTHETIC_AUDIO_BYTES)} bytes WAV)\")\n","print(f\"  Canonical Chunks   : {len(expected_windows)}\")\n","print(f\"  Packaged Score     : {s_pkg:.12f} (assessment: '{res_pkg.result.assessment}')\")\n","print(f\"  Legacy Score       : {s_leg:.12f} (assessment: '{res_leg.result.assessment}')\")\n","print(f\"  Absolute Delta     : {score_diff:.2e}\")\n","print(f\"  Exact Bitwise Equiv: {exact_match}\")\n","print(f\"  Max Chunk Delta    : {max_chunk_diff:.2e}\")\n","print(f\"  Chunk Scores (Pkg) : {[round(c, 8) for c in res_pkg.chunk_scores]}\")\n","print(f\"  Chunk Scores (Leg) : {[round(c, 8) for c in res_leg.chunk_scores]}\")\n","\n","PARITY_TOLERANCE = 1e-9\n","assert score_diff <= PARITY_TOLERANCE, f\"Score difference {score_diff} exceeds tolerance {PARITY_TOLERANCE}\"\n","assert max_chunk_diff <= PARITY_TOLERANCE, f\"Chunk score difference {max_chunk_diff} exceeds tolerance\"\n","assert res_pkg.result.status == \"success\", \"Packaged inference status not success\"\n","assert res_leg.result.status == \"success\", \"Legacy inference status not success\"\n","assert res_pkg.result.assessment == res_leg.result.assessment, \"Assessment mismatch\"\n","assert res_pkg.result.model_version == res_leg.result.model_version == \"logistic_regression:B\"\n","\n","STAGE_RESULTS[\"Stage H (Scoring Parity)\"] = {\n","    \"status\": \"PASS\",\n","    \"details\": f\"Bit-for-bit parity verified (|diff|={score_diff:.2e} <= {PARITY_TOLERANCE}, exact={exact_match}, 2 chunks)\"\n","}"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"n2_000018","metadata":{"id":"n2_000018"},"source":["## Stage I — Threshold Behavior and Decision Rule Semantics\n","\n","This stage verifies the threshold resolution contract across both packaged and legacy loaders:\n","1. **Default inheritance:** Packaged bundle uses its stored threshold (`0.5`) when no override is passed.\n","2. **Override behavior:** An explicit threshold parameter (e.g. `threshold=0.75`) overrides the decision rule in the loaded bundle without modifying `bundle.json` on disk.\n","3. **Legacy behavior:** Legacy loading defaults to `0.5`, and respects explicit threshold overrides.\n","4. **Validation:** Invalid numeric thresholds ($< 0.0$, $> 1.0$) raise `ContractError`. Non-numeric thresholds are rejected with `ValueError`/`TypeError` by `load_lr_bundle()` and with `ContractError` by `DecisionRule`.\n","5. **Score invariance:** Threshold changes affect only the decision boundary (`result.assessment`), never the underlying raw model score or weights."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":51,"id":"n2_000019","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"n2_000019","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794109438730,"user_tz":-300,"elapsed":383,"user":{"displayName":"MUHAMMADNOUMAN FAZIL","userId":"00466758265510267650"}},"outputId":"d9cc194a-2a00-4259-c165-e8db7e4d5c9a"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["[Threshold Behavior Validation]\n","  Packaged Default Threshold  : 0.5\n","  Packaged Override Threshold : 0.75\n","  Disk Stored Threshold       : 0.5 (preserved)\n","  Legacy Default Threshold    : 0.5\n","  Legacy Override Threshold   : 0.8\n","  Out-of-range Rejection      : ContractError verified on [-0.1, 1.05, 2.0]\n","  Non-numeric Rejection       : Verified (load_lr_bundle rejects ValueError/TypeError; DecisionRule rejects ContractError)\n","  Raw Score at t=0.50         : 0.999958552420 (assessment: 'synthetic')\n","  Raw Score at t=0.75         : 0.999958552420 (assessment: 'synthetic')\n","  Raw Score Invariance        : True\n"]}],"source":["from echoproof.contracts import ContractError, DecisionRule\n","\n","# 1. Packaged default vs override\n","b_pkg_default = load_lr_bundle(BUNDLE_DIR)\n","b_pkg_override = load_lr_bundle(BUNDLE_DIR, threshold=0.75)\n","\n","assert b_pkg_default.spec.decision_rule.threshold == 0.5\n","assert b_pkg_override.spec.decision_rule.threshold == 0.75\n","\n","# Verify disk bundle.json is untouched\n","disk_manifest = json.loads(BUNDLE_JSON_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n","assert disk_manifest[\"decision_rule\"][\"threshold\"] == 0.5, \"Disk bundle.json was modified by threshold override!\"\n","\n","# 2. Legacy default vs override\n","b_leg_default = load_lr_bundle(ORIG_MODEL_DIR)\n","b_leg_override = load_lr_bundle(ORIG_MODEL_DIR, threshold=0.80)\n","\n","assert b_leg_default.spec.decision_rule.threshold == 0.5\n","assert b_leg_override.spec.decision_rule.threshold == 0.80\n","\n","# 3. Invalid threshold rejection\n","# 3a. Out-of-range numeric thresholds rejected by DecisionRule with ContractError\n","invalid_numeric_thresholds = [-0.1, 1.05, 2.0]\n","for bad_t in invalid_numeric_thresholds:\n","    try:\n","        load_lr_bundle(BUNDLE_DIR, threshold=bad_t)\n","        raise AssertionError(f\"Expected ContractError for threshold {bad_t}\")\n","    except ContractError:\n","        pass  # expected\n","\n","# 3b. Non-numeric thresholds rejected by load_lr_bundle production API with ValueError/TypeError\n","non_numeric_thresholds = [\"non_numeric\", [0.5], {\"threshold\": 0.5}]\n","for bad_val in non_numeric_thresholds:\n","    try:\n","        load_lr_bundle(BUNDLE_DIR, threshold=bad_val)\n","        raise AssertionError(f\"Expected ValueError/TypeError for non-numeric threshold: {bad_val!r}\")\n","    except (ValueError, TypeError):\n","        pass  # expected rejection by production API float conversion\n","\n","# 3c. Direct contract validation: DecisionRule rejects non-numeric threshold with ContractError\n","try:\n","    DecisionRule(schema_version=1, kind=\"threshold\", threshold=\"non_numeric\")  # type: ignore\n","    raise AssertionError(\"Expected ContractError from DecisionRule for non-numeric threshold\")\n","except ContractError:\n","    pass  # expected rejection by contract schema validation\n","\n","# 4. Raw score invariance under threshold changes\n","res_t50 = analyze(SYNTHETIC_AUDIO_BYTES, b_pkg_default)\n","res_t75 = analyze(SYNTHETIC_AUDIO_BYTES, b_pkg_override)\n","\n","print(\"[Threshold Behavior Validation]\")\n","print(f\"  Packaged Default Threshold  : {b_pkg_default.spec.decision_rule.threshold}\")\n","print(f\"  Packaged Override Threshold : {b_pkg_override.spec.decision_rule.threshold}\")\n","print(f\"  Disk Stored Threshold       : {disk_manifest['decision_rule']['threshold']} (preserved)\")\n","print(f\"  Legacy Default Threshold    : {b_leg_default.spec.decision_rule.threshold}\")\n","print(f\"  Legacy Override Threshold   : {b_leg_override.spec.decision_rule.threshold}\")\n","print(f\"  Out-of-range Rejection      : ContractError verified on {invalid_numeric_thresholds}\")\n","print(f\"  Non-numeric Rejection       : Verified (load_lr_bundle rejects ValueError/TypeError; DecisionRule rejects ContractError)\")\n","print(f\"  Raw Score at t=0.50         : {res_t50.result.score:.12f} (assessment: '{res_t50.result.assessment}')\")\n","print(f\"  Raw Score at t=0.75         : {res_t75.result.score:.12f} (assessment: '{res_t75.result.assessment}')\")\n","print(f\"  Raw Score Invariance        : {res_t50.result.score == res_t75.result.score}\")\n","\n","assert res_t50.result.score == res_t75.result.score, \"Raw score changed when adjusting decision threshold!\"\n","\n","STAGE_RESULTS[\"Stage I (Threshold Behavior)\"] = {\n","    \"status\": \"PASS\",\n","    \"details\": \"Threshold defaults, overrides, disk immutability, out-of-range & non-numeric rejection, and score invariance verified\"\n","}"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"n2_000020","metadata":{"id":"n2_000020"},"source":["## Stage J — Negative Integrity Tests (Isolated Sandboxes)\n","\n","This stage validates that the integrity protections in `load_bundle()` and `validate_lock_record()` reliably detect and reject tampered or corrupted artifacts.\n","\n","### Safety Guarantee\n","All negative tests operate strictly inside **temporary isolated directories** (`tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()`). The original production bundle, lock record, and source artifacts are never modified.\n","\n","### Test Scenarios\n","1. **Component Checksum Corruption:** Modify bytes in `model/weights.npz` $\\rightarrow$ `BundleError` (checksum mismatch).\n","2. **Metadata Tampering:** Alter `bundle.json` $\\rightarrow$ `LockError` (`bundle_metadata_hash` mismatch).\n","3. **Missing Component:** Delete `model/lr_model.json` $\\rightarrow$ `BundleError` (missing component file).\n","4. **Lock Component Checksum Tampering:** Alter recorded SHA-256 in lock $\\rightarrow$ `LockError` (component hash mismatch).\n","5. **Evidence Tampering & Generator Rejection:** Alter bytes and task/protocol metadata in temporary copy of `evidence.json` $\\rightarrow$ independent SHA-256 divergence detected, and `generate_protocol_b_lock()` fails with `LockError`.\n","6. **Post-Test Verification:** Confirm production artifacts remain 100% intact."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":52,"id":"n2_000021","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"n2_000021","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794109442717,"user_tz":-300,"elapsed":115,"user":{"displayName":"MUHAMMADNOUMAN FAZIL","userId":"00466758265510267650"}},"outputId":"2c0ac7dd-4e9f-499c-d301-469bd745805e"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["[Negative Integrity Tests in Isolated Sandboxes]\n","  - Corrupted component bytes       : [PASS] (load_bundle caught checksum mismatch)\n","  - Metadata tampering              : [PASS] (validate_lock_record caught metadata hash mismatch)\n","  - Missing component file          : [PASS] (load_bundle caught missing component)\n","  - Lock component hash tampering   : [PASS] (validate_lock_record caught component hash mismatch)\n","  - Evidence file tampering         : [PASS] (Detected digest divergence and generate_protocol_b_lock rejected tampered evidence)\n","\n","[Post-Test Production Check] Original bundle and lock remain 100% intact and valid.\n"]}],"source":["from echoproof.bundle import BundleError\n","from echoproof.lock import generate_protocol_b_lock\n","\n","negative_results = []\n","\n","with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as temp_sandbox:\n","    sandbox_dir = Path(temp_sandbox)\n","\n","    # 1. Corrupted component bytes\n","    corrupt_bundle_dir = sandbox_dir / \"bundle_corrupt\"\n","    shutil.copytree(BUNDLE_DIR, corrupt_bundle_dir)\n","    (corrupt_bundle_dir / \"model\" / \"weights.npz\").write_bytes(b\"corrupted_weights_payload\")\n","    try:\n","        load_bundle(corrupt_bundle_dir)\n","        test1_pass = False\n","    except BundleError as e:\n","        test1_pass = (\"Checksum mismatch\" in str(e))\n","    negative_results.append((\"Corrupted component bytes\", test1_pass, \"load_bundle caught checksum mismatch\"))\n","\n","    # 2. Metadata tampering (lock metadata hash mismatch)\n","    tamper_bundle_dir = sandbox_dir / \"bundle_tamper_meta\"\n","    shutil.copytree(BUNDLE_DIR, tamper_bundle_dir)\n","    tamper_meta = json.loads((tamper_bundle_dir / \"bundle.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n","    tamper_meta[\"model_version\"] = \"logistic_regression:B_tampered\"\n","    (tamper_bundle_dir / \"bundle.json\").write_text(json.dumps(tamper_meta, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n","    try:\n","        validate_lock_record(lock_record, bundle_dir=tamper_bundle_dir)\n","        test2_pass = False\n","    except LockError as e:\n","        test2_pass = (\"bundle_metadata_hash mismatch\" in str(e))\n","    negative_results.append((\"Metadata tampering\", test2_pass, \"validate_lock_record caught metadata hash mismatch\"))\n","\n","    # 3. Missing component file\n","    missing_bundle_dir = sandbox_dir / \"bundle_missing_comp\"\n","    shutil.copytree(BUNDLE_DIR, missing_bundle_dir)\n","    (missing_bundle_dir / \"model\" / \"lr_model.json\").unlink()\n","    try:\n","        load_bundle(missing_bundle_dir)\n","        test3_pass = False\n","    except BundleError as e:\n","        test3_pass = (\"Missing bundle component file\" in str(e))\n","    negative_results.append((\"Missing component file\", test3_pass, \"load_bundle caught missing component\"))\n","\n","    # 4. Lock component hash tampering\n","    tampered_lock = json.loads(json.dumps(lock_record))\n","    tampered_lock[\"bundle\"][\"components\"][\"model/weights.npz\"][\"sha256\"] = \"0\" * 64\n","    try:\n","        validate_lock_record(tampered_lock, bundle_dir=BUNDLE_DIR)\n","        test4_pass = False\n","    except LockError as e:\n","        test4_pass = (\"Component hash mismatch\" in str(e))\n","    negative_results.append((\"Lock component hash tampering\", test4_pass, \"validate_lock_record caught component hash mismatch\"))\n","\n","    # 5. Evidence file tampering:\n","    # 5a. Detect SHA-256 divergence against lock's recorded evidence hash\n","    tampered_ev_bytes = ORIG_EVIDENCE_PATH.read_bytes() + b\"\\n/* tampered */\"\n","    tampered_ev_file = sandbox_dir / \"tampered_evidence.json\"\n","    tampered_ev_file.write_bytes(tampered_ev_bytes)\n","    tampered_ev_hash = hashlib.sha256(tampered_ev_bytes).hexdigest()\n","    hash_diverged = (tampered_ev_hash != lock_evidence_sha)\n","\n","    # 5b. Verify generate_protocol_b_lock fails when evidence content is tampered (wrong protocol)\n","    tampered_ev_json = json.loads(ORIG_EVIDENCE_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n","    tampered_ev_json[\"protocol\"] = \"TAMPERED_PROTOCOL\"\n","    bad_protocol_file = sandbox_dir / \"bad_protocol_evidence.json\"\n","    bad_protocol_file.write_text(json.dumps(tampered_ev_json), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n","    try:\n","        generate_protocol_b_lock(\n","            bundle_dir=BUNDLE_DIR,\n","            evidence_path=bad_protocol_file,\n","            output_path=sandbox_dir / \"tampered_lock.json\"\n","        )\n","        gen_rejected = False\n","    except LockError as e:\n","        gen_rejected = (\"Expected evidence protocol 'B'\" in str(e))\n","\n","    test5_pass = hash_diverged and gen_rejected\n","    negative_results.append((\"Evidence file tampering\", test5_pass, \"Detected digest divergence and generate_protocol_b_lock rejected tampered evidence\"))\n","\n","print(\"[Negative Integrity Tests in Isolated Sandboxes]\")\n","for name, passed, detail in negative_results:\n","    status_str = \"PASS\" if passed else \"FAIL\"\n","    print(f\"  - {name:<32}: [{status_str}] ({detail})\")\n","    assert passed, f\"Negative integrity test failed: {name}\"\n","\n","# Verify production artifacts remain intact\n","check_bundle = load_bundle(BUNDLE_DIR)\n","check_lock = load_lock_record(LOCK_PATH, bundle_dir=BUNDLE_DIR)\n","assert check_bundle.spec.bundle_id == \"bundle:r2-lr-protocol-b\"\n","assert check_lock[\"lock_id\"] == \"lock:protocol_b_lr_v1\"\n","print(\"\\n[Post-Test Production Check] Original bundle and lock remain 100% intact and valid.\")\n","\n","STAGE_RESULTS[\"Stage J (Negative Integrity Tests)\"] = {\n","    \"status\": \"PASS\",\n","    \"details\": f\"All {len(negative_results)} negative integrity sandboxes passed; production artifacts unmodified\"\n","}"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"n2_000022","metadata":{"id":"n2_000022"},"source":["## Stage K — Regression Test Suite Execution\n","\n","This stage executes the actual repository test suites via `unittest`:\n","- `tests/test_r2_bundle.py`: Bundle writer, loader, failure-safe staging, and integrity tests.\n","- `tests/test_r2_lock.py`: Protocol B lock generator, validator, audit verification, and range checks.\n","- `tests/test_r2_n1_integration.py`: End-to-end integration and parity tests across CLI, Evaluator, and App.\n","\n","### Execution Policy\n","- Discovers and executes actual tests using `unittest.TextTestRunner`.\n","- Records test count, passes, failures, and errors.\n","- Never reports PASS if zero tests were discovered or if any suite encountered errors."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":53,"id":"n2_000023","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"n2_000023","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794109462850,"user_tz":-300,"elapsed":15686,"user":{"displayName":"MUHAMMADNOUMAN FAZIL","userId":"00466758265510267650"}},"outputId":"47a49c2f-9e82-448f-a9a6-a9f3b476ad01"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["[Executing Repository Regression Suites]\n","\n","======================================================================\n","test_r2_bundle: PASS\n","test_bundle_write_and_load_roundtrip (test_r2_bundle.TestBundleWriterAndLoader.test_bundle_write_and_load_roundtrip) ... ok\n","test_checksum_mismatch_rejection (test_r2_bundle.TestBundleWriterAndLoader.test_checksum_mismatch_rejection) ... ok\n","test_failure_safe_overwrite_preserves_original_on_error (test_r2_bundle.TestBundleWriterAndLoader.test_failure_safe_overwrite_preserves_original_on_error) ... ok\n","test_invalid_metadata_rejection (test_r2_bundle.TestBundleWriterAndLoader.test_invalid_metadata_rejection) ... ok\n","test_load_lr_bundle_preprocessing_hash_mismatch_raises (test_r2_bundle.TestBundleWriterAndLoader.test_load_lr_bundle_preprocessing_hash_mismatch_raises) ... ok\n","test_load_lr_bundle_with_verified_bundle_and_threshold_override (test_r2_bundle.TestBundleWriterAndLoader.test_load_lr_bundle_with_verif